RSX shadow compare: the function is depth FUNC reference, not reference FUNC depth (open upstream PR, imported as is).

Resistance 3 samples its Z16 shadow maps with GEQUAL. With the toolkit's reference FUNC depth order every shadowed
light comes out inverted: the floor under the Home level's hanging lamp and the sofa beside it get no light, and the
whole level is far darker than on the console. The reversed order is RPCS3's (VKDraw.cpp, get_compare_func(zfunc, true);
GLDraw: "the stored texture function is reversed"). It looked wrong here before gcm-rsx/0008 only because the material
pass read the light buffer at twice the pixel position: more light, more visible ghosts.

Scripted run (Home level, CHAPTER ONE view): the lit pool under the lamp and on the sofa appears as in the console
screenshots; no ghosts or bands with 0008 on. test_shadow_compare_metal.m is in the PR.

Upstream: PR #424 (drop this file when the pin contains it).
